{
 "about": "The cinema shuffler for Mexico (Josh, 2026-11-09: \"a mexican film area… feature to feature like Italy… start with 50 mexican films and expand through more ideas\"; \"copy the italy code as much as possible\"). Built like Italy's: Mexican films chosen in the cloud session, checked with scripts/cinema-check-films.mjs (LANG_CODE=es REGION=MX: TMDB's Mexican-Spanish title, poster, videos with Spanish first; fullFilm is a full-length YouTube upload found by searching YouTube, checked by title and running time, playable in other apps). Adults-only films are left out. Shelf titles are shown as written. The rule (Josh, 2026-11-06, agreed for Italy): a film is in only with at least one video in the learned language, its trailer or the full film. TMDB's language labels are unreliable and YouTube won't say from the cloud, so until the laptop runs scripts/cinema-video-language.mjs and scripts/cinema-apply-language.mjs (COUNTRY=es-mx), films whose only Spanish may be unheard are included pending that check. Josh, 2026-11-09 (rule 3): a film originally made in Spanish (`original: \"es\"`) counts its full upload as Spanish when the audio couldn't be heard, unless the upload's title says it's dubbed; scripts/cinema-apply-language.mjs applies it. Ten films came back this way.",
